<section id="membaca-wayang" class="section heritage-section motif-perforation">
  <div class="heritage-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span data-lang-content="id">ADEGAN 02B · MEMBACA WAYANG</span><span data-lang-content="en">SCENE 02B · READING WAYANG</span></p>
    <h2><span data-lang-content="id">Bukan sekadar boneka: sebuah bahasa panggung.</span><span data-lang-content="en">Not simply puppets: a language for the stage.</span></h2>
    <p data-lang-content="id">Gunakan empat lensa berikut saat membaca koleksi. Ini adalah pengantar interpretatif yang membantu pengunjung mengamati objek, bukan pengganti label museum atau penjelasan pemandu.</p>
    <p data-lang-content="en">Use these four lenses when reading the collection. They are an interpretive introduction to help visitors observe objects, not a substitute for museum labels or a guide’s explanation.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wayang-primer-grid">
    <article class="primer-card"><span class="card-number">01</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Layar & cahaya</span><span data-lang-content="en">Screen & light</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Pada wayang kulit, bentuk datar dari kulit digerakkan di depan kelir atau layar yang diterangi dari belakang. Bayangan adalah bagian dari bahasa pertunjukan, bukan sekadar efek visual.</p><p data-lang-content="en">In wayang kulit, flat leather figures move before a kelir, or screen, lit from behind. The shadow is part of the performance language, not merely a visual effect.</p></article>
    <article class="primer-card"><span class="card-number">02</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Bahan & bentuk</span><span data-lang-content="en">Material & form</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Wayang kulit, wayang golek, dan bentuk tiga dimensi lain dibedakan oleh bahan, siluet, teknik gerak, serta konteks daerahnya. Jangan menganggap seluruh wayang sebagai satu tradisi yang seragam.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Wayang kulit, wayang golek, and other three-dimensional forms differ in material, silhouette, movement, and regional setting. Avoid treating all wayang as one uniform tradition.</p></article>
    <article class="primer-card"><span class="card-number">03</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Dalang & ansambel</span><span data-lang-content="en">Dalang & ensemble</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Dalang menghidupkan tokoh dan alur; penyanyi serta pemusik membangun ritme dan suasana. Museum dapat dibaca sebagai jejak praktik kolaboratif, bukan sekadar deretan artefak.</p><p data-lang-content="en">The dalang animates characters and story; singers and musicians build rhythm and atmosphere. The museum can be read as evidence of a collaborative practice, not simply a line of artefacts.</p></article>
    <article class="primer-card"><span class="card-number">04</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Cerita & nilai</span><span data-lang-content="en">Story & values</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Repertoar dapat meminjam tokoh dari epos India, kisah lokal, dan tradisi lain. Humor dan tokoh rakyat juga dapat membuka ruang untuk komentar sosial; setiap pertunjukan memiliki gaya sendiri.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Repertoires can draw characters from Indian epics, local stories, and other traditions. Humour and ordinary-person characters can also make room for social commentary; every performance has its own style.</p></article>
  </div>
  <div class="myth-note"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span data-lang-content="id">CATATAN KONTEKS</span><span data-lang-content="en">CONTEXT NOTE</span></p><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Cerita, tradisi, dan sejarah bukan hal yang sama.</span><span data-lang-content="en">Story, tradition, and historical record are not the same thing.</span></h3></div><p data-lang-content="id">Kisah Ramayana, Mahabharata, cerita Panji, dan ragam narasi lain dapat hadir dalam dunia pewayangan, tetapi versi, tokoh, dan penekanannya berubah menurut daerah, komunitas, dan dalang. Situs ini memperlakukan cerita tersebut sebagai warisan pertunjukan dan interpretasi budaya—bukan sebagai klaim fakta sejarah tunggal.</p><p data-lang-content="en">The Ramayana, Mahabharata, Panji stories, and other narratives can appear in wayang worlds, but versions, characters, and emphases change among regions, communities, and dalang. This site treats them as performance heritage and cultural interpretation—not as a single claim of historical fact.</p></div>
  <p class="source-note"><span data-lang-content="id">Rujukan konteks: </span><span data-lang-content="en">Context sources: </span><a href="https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/wayang-puppet-theatre-00063" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage</a> · <a href="https://mitramuseumjakarta.id/wayang" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Museum Wayang institutional profile</a></p>
</section>

<section id="transport-detail" class="section practice-section motif-arch">
  <p class="eyebrow"><span data-lang-content="id">ADEGAN 04B · DETAIL PERJALANAN</span><span data-lang-content="en">SCENE 04B · JOURNEY DETAIL</span></p>
  <div class="service-heading"><div><h2><span data-lang-content="id">Pilih rute, lalu cek kondisi saat itu.</span><span data-lang-content="en">Choose a route, then check conditions live.</span></h2></div><p data-lang-content="id">Waktu, tarif, rekayasa lalu lintas, dan titik naik/turun dapat berubah. Informasi berikut menjelaskan cara mempertimbangkan setiap moda tanpa mengarahkan pada penyedia komersial tertentu.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Times, fares, traffic arrangements, and pick-up or drop-off points can change. These notes explain how to weigh each mode without directing visitors to any commercial provider.</p></div>
  <div class="travel-modes">
    <article class="travel-card"><span class="card-number">01</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Bandara</span><span data-lang-content="en">Airport</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Dari Soekarno–Hatta, kereta bandara atau bus bandara dapat digunakan untuk tahap pertama menuju pusat kota; menuju Kota Tua biasanya membutuhkan perpindahan tambahan. Jika membawa barang banyak, tiba larut, atau bepergian bersama keluarga, bandingkan dengan taksi resmi atau kendaraan daring dari titik penjemputan yang diizinkan.</p><p data-lang-content="en">From Soekarno–Hatta, airport rail or airport bus can be used for the first leg toward central Jakarta; reaching Kota Tua usually requires an additional transfer. With heavy luggage, a late arrival, or family travel, compare this with an official taxi or ride-hailing car from an authorized pick-up point.</p></article>
    <article class="travel-card"><span class="card-number">02</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Commuter Line</span><span data-lang-content="en">Commuter Line</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Stasiun Jakarta Kota adalah titik kereta terdekat yang dicantumkan museum, dengan rujukan jalan kaki sekitar 300 m ke arah timur laut. Cek peta rute, jadwal, dan kondisi stasiun KAI Commuter pada hari perjalanan.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Jakarta Kota Station is the museum-listed nearest rail point, with a referenced walk of about 300 m to the north-east. Check KAI Commuter’s route map, timetable, and station conditions on your travel day.</p></article>
    <article class="travel-card"><span class="card-number">03</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">TransJakarta & mikrolet</span><span data-lang-content="en">TransJakarta & Mikrolet</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Museum menyebut Halte Kali Besar Barat sekitar 230 m ke selatan dan Halte Jakarta Kota sekitar 500 m ke utara. Rujukan mikrolet yang tercantum adalah M08, M12, M15/15A, dan M25 menuju Kota; cek operasi aktif sebelum berangkat.</p><p data-lang-content="en">The museum lists Kali Besar Barat Stop about 230 m south and Jakarta Kota Stop about 500 m north. Its listed Mikrolet references are M08, M12, M15/15A, and M25 toward Kota; check active service before departure.</p></article>
    <article class="travel-card"><span class="card-number">04</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Taksi & kendaraan daring</span><span data-lang-content="en">Taxi & ride-hailing</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Atur titik turun di sekitar Jalan Pintu Besar Utara, lalu lanjutkan sesuai pengaturan pejalan kaki. Untuk pulang, pilih titik jemput setelah keluar dari arus pengunjung; periksa pelat nomor, tarif, dan keselamatan perjalanan sendiri.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Set a drop-off near Jalan Pintu Besar Utara, then continue with local pedestrian arrangements. For the return, choose a meeting point after clearing visitor flow; independently verify number plates, fares, and travel safety.</p></article>
    <article class="travel-card"><span class="card-number">05</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Mobil, motor & parkir</span><span data-lang-content="en">Car, motor & parking</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Museum menyebut area parkir Jalan Cengkeh dan Kali Besar. Kapasitas, akses kendaraan, serta aturan parkir dapat berubah terutama pada akhir pekan dan acara kawasan; pertimbangkan datang lebih awal atau menggunakan angkutan umum.</p><p data-lang-content="en">The museum cites Jalan Cengkeh and Kali Besar parking areas. Capacity, vehicle access, and parking rules can change, especially at weekends and during district events; consider arriving early or using public transport.</p></article>
  </div>
  <div class="arrival-note"><strong><span data-lang-content="id">RUJUKAN AKTIF</span><span data-lang-content="en">LIVE CHECKS</span></strong><span data-lang-content="id">Gunakan <a href="https://kci.id/perjalanan-krl/peta-rute" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">peta rute KAI Commuter</a>, kanal operator bus, dan peta langsung untuk mengonfirmasi rute, gangguan, akses pejalan kaki, serta titik jemput aktual.</span><span data-lang-content="en">Use the <a href="https://kci.id/perjalanan-krl/peta-rute" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">KAI Commuter route map</a>, bus-operator channels, and a live map to confirm routes, disruptions, pedestrian access, and current pick-up points.</span></div>
</section>

<section id="layanan" class="section service-guide motif-shadow-frame">
  <div class="service-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span data-lang-content="id">SEKITAR KOTA TUA</span><span data-lang-content="en">AROUND KOTA TUA</span></p><h2><span data-lang-content="id">Kebutuhan praktis, dijelaskan secara netral.</span><span data-lang-content="en">Practical needs, explained neutrally.</span></h2></div><p data-lang-content="id">Bagian ini menunjuk jenis layanan yang lazim dicari pengunjung, bukan merekomendasikan atau menilai satu usaha. Gunakan peta langsung, jam buka, dan kebutuhan pribadi untuk memilih tempat yang sesuai.</p><p data-lang-content="en">This section points to service types visitors commonly need; it does not recommend or rank any business. Use a live map, opening hours, and personal requirements to choose an appropriate option.</p></div>
  <div class="service-grid">
    <article class="service-card"><span class="card-number">01</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">WC, ibadah & istirahat</span><span data-lang-content="en">WC, prayer & rest</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Museum mencantumkan toilet dan musholla. Untuk perjalanan panjang, perhatikan lokasi toilet umum, tempat duduk, air minum, dan perlindungan dari panas atau hujan sebelum meninggalkan kawasan museum.</p><p data-lang-content="en">The museum lists toilets and a prayer room. On a longer day, note public toilets, seating, drinking water, and shelter from heat or rain before leaving the museum area.</p></article>
    <article class="service-card"><span class="card-number">02</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Makan & minum</span><span data-lang-content="en">Food & drink</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Cari warung, kedai kopi, kafe, atau restoran berdasarkan preferensi diet, sanitasi, harga, jam buka, dan jarak berjalan kaki. Bawa air minum bila cuaca panas.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Look for food stalls, coffee shops, cafés, or restaurants based on dietary preference, sanitation, price, opening hours, and walking distance. Carry water in hot weather.</p></article>
    <article class="service-card"><span class="card-number">03</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Menginap</span><span data-lang-content="en">Accommodation</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Pilihan yang relevan dapat berupa hotel, wisma, atau penginapan jangka pendek. Bandingkan akses transportasi, keamanan berjalan kaki malam hari, kebijakan check-in, dan kebutuhan aksesibilitas.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Relevant options can include hotels, guesthouses, or short-stay accommodation. Compare transport access, nighttime walking safety, check-in policies, and accessibility needs.</p></article>
    <article class="service-card"><span class="card-number">04</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Belanja harian & uang tunai</span><span data-lang-content="en">Daily supplies & cash</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Gunakan peta untuk mencari minimarket, toko kebutuhan harian, ATM, atau layanan pembayaran yang sesuai rute Anda. Periksa apakah kartu, tunai, atau pembayaran digital diterima sebelum berbelanja.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Use a map to locate convenience stores, daily-supply shops, ATMs, or payment services along your route. Check whether cards, cash, or digital payments are accepted before buying.</p></article>
    <article class="service-card"><span class="card-number">05</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Bahan bakar & pengisian</span><span data-lang-content="en">Fuel & charging</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Bagi pengendara, rencanakan SPBU atau titik pengisian kendaraan listrik dari peta berdasarkan arah masuk dan keluar kota tua. Ketersediaan konektor, antrean, atau akses kendaraan tidak dijamin; periksa sebelum bergerak.</p><p data-lang-content="en">For drivers, plan fuel stations or EV charging from a map according to your old-town entry and exit. Connector availability, queues, and vehicle access are not guaranteed; check before setting out.</p></article>
    <article class="service-card"><span class="card-number">06</span><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Bantuan & kebutuhan khusus</span><span data-lang-content="en">Help & specific needs</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Untuk apotek, klinik, ATM, ruang keluarga, atau kebutuhan mobilitas, gunakan peta langsung dan hubungi penyedia layanan bila perlu. Pengunjung dengan kebutuhan akses khusus disarankan menghubungi museum sebelum berangkat.</p><p data-lang-content="en">For pharmacies, clinics, cash access, family facilities, or mobility needs, use a live map and contact providers where needed. Visitors with specific access needs are advised to contact the museum before travel.</p></article>
  </div>
  <div class="neutral-note"><b><span data-lang-content="id">KEBIJAKAN NETRAL</span><span data-lang-content="en">NEUTRALITY POLICY</span></b><p data-lang-content="id">Museum Wayang Guide tidak menerima bayaran untuk menampilkan usaha dan tidak memberi peringkat, afiliasi, atau rekomendasi komersial. Informasi layanan disusun sebagai orientasi praktis, bukan endorsement.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Museum Wayang Guide does not accept payment to feature businesses and gives no rankings, affiliations, or commercial recommendations. Service information is practical orientation, not an endorsement.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="section practice-section motif-arch">
  <p class="eyebrow"><span data-lang-content="id">KUNJUNGAN YANG BERTANGGUNG JAWAB</span><span data-lang-content="en">A RESPONSIBLE VISIT</span></p>
  <div class="section-heading"><h2><span data-lang-content="id">Baca pelan-pelan, bergerak dengan sadar.</span><span data-lang-content="en">Look slowly, move thoughtfully.</span></h2><p data-lang-content="id">Pengalaman museum lebih baik saat kebutuhan praktis, ruang bersama, dan koleksi sama-sama diperhatikan.</p><p data-lang-content="en">A museum visit works better when practical needs, shared space, and the collection receive equal care.</p></div>
  <div class="practice-grid">
    <article><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Sebelum tiba</span><span data-lang-content="en">Before arrival</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Konfirmasi jam, tiket, cuaca, transportasi pulang, dan kebutuhan akses. Jika membawa anak-anak atau rombongan, sepakati titik berkumpul dan waktu istirahat.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Confirm hours, tickets, weather, return transport, and access needs. With children or a group, agree on a meeting point and rest time.</p></article>
    <article><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Di dalam museum</span><span data-lang-content="en">Inside the museum</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Jaga jarak dari objek, baca label sebelum memotret, dan beri ruang pada pengunjung lain. Tanyakan kepada staf bila ragu mengenai koleksi, rute, atau aturan ruang.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Keep a distance from objects, read labels before photographing, and leave room for other visitors. Ask staff when unsure about a collection, route, or room rule.</p></article>
    <article><h3><span data-lang-content="id">Setelah berkunjung</span><span data-lang-content="en">After the visit</span></h3><p data-lang-content="id">Catat informasi yang berubah dan gunakan tombol masukan untuk mengirim koreksi bersumber. Dengan begitu panduan komunitas dapat terus diperbarui tanpa mengiklankan pihak tertentu.</p><p data-lang-content="en">Note information that has changed and use the feedback link to send sourced corrections. This helps a community guide remain current without advertising any party.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
